+  "consequence": "wall ratios near 1.00 are inside the noise and must NOT be read as small real effects. The 12 vacuous rows time at 0.00-0.02 s and carry no timing signal at all.",
+  "floor_MEASURED_in_the_sibling_harness_2026_07_30": {
+   "how": "a trailing-control arm was added to scripts/arc_state_key_dedup_xgame_verify.py: the control key is re-run LAST, so leading/trailing is an A/A over identical work differing only in position. Partition identity between the two was asserted, so the ratio is pure timing drift.",
+   "per_game_drift_x": {
