+   "THE_DECISIVE_CONSEQUENCE_FOR_THIS_PHASE": "L1's 1.021x median WALL reduction -- and 13 of 14 strong rows, all under 1.08x -- sit DEEP INSIDE a 10.8-14.6% floor. On this evidence the deployable branching cut is not measurably faster at all across the corpus; only ka59's 1.210x approaches the floor's edge, and even that is barely outside it. This is the strongest single reason not to ship the branching cut, and it is stronger than the completeness argument: the lever may simply not do anything worth measuring.",
